    "root_cause_category": "config_or_deploy_change",
    "explanation": "At 14:01 the deploy of checkout-api 2026.11.3 raised WORKER_CONCURRENCY from 8 to 32 (LOG-0001-0006, LOG-0001-0007). The orders-db client pool stayed at 20 connections (LOG-0001-0008). Before the deploy the pool was using 6 of 20 connections with nothing waiting (LOG-0001-0003). Right after it, usage climbed to 17 with requests queuing (LOG-0001-0013), then the pool filled completely and the queue kept growing (LOG-0001-0016, LOG-0001-0038). Connection acquires started timing out after 3 s and requests failed with 503s (LOG-0001-0023, LOG-0001-0024), which is the latency breach the alert fired on (LOG-0001-0036). The database itself was fine: 20 of 200 sessions in use and 23% CPU (LOG-0001-0025). All six instances stayed healthy, and the session-cache miss spike was just cache warming that recovered by 14:04:58 (LOG-0001-0014), so neither caused this. I didn't check the RB-DB-POOL runbook. Rolling back the concurrency change, or sizing the pool to match it, should end the incident.",
